### The Kotlin standard library

The Android agent's dex, which the daemon embeds (`agent-android/build.sh`), holds the parts of the Kotlin standard library that R8 keeps: kotlin-stdlib 2.4.20, Copyright 2010-2024 JetBrains s.r.o. and Kotlin Programming Language contributors, under the Apache License 2.0, whose text is under [Crates](#crates).

### The Android emulator's controller protocol

`crates/android/proto/emulator_controller.proto`, which the Android driver compiles into its gRPC client: Copyright (C) 2018 The Android Open Source Project, under the Apache License 2.0, whose text is under [Crates](#crates).

### The fixtures

The reference apps under `fixtures/` are built on a developer's machine and never shipped. The Expo fixture starts from Expo's template, whose MIT license `fixtures/expo/LICENSE` keeps, and installs its npm packages from `fixtures/expo/bun.lock` when it is built; the Compose fixture's Android libraries come through Gradle when it is built, and its Gradle wrapper (`fixtures/compose/gradlew`, `gradlew.bat` and `gradle/wrapper/`) is the Gradle project's, under the Apache License 2.0; the SwiftUI fixture uses Apple's SDK alone. The iPhone runner's bundle is built the same way, from Xcode's `XCTRunner.app`, and is not in the repository.

